Description:
  forge — Mission Control Language runtime

Usage:
  forge [command] [options]

Options:
  -?, -h, --help  Show help and usage information
  --version       Show version information

Commands:
  init <mission>             Resolve expert sources and generate mcl.lock
  run <mission>              Run a mission
  validate <mission>         Validate a mission file and its expert references
  list                       List available resources
  expert                     Manage experts
  registry                   OCI registry operations
  login                      Sign in to Forge (browser) and store a platform key
  whoami                     Show the signed-in Forge user and credit balance
  logout                     Sign out of Forge (remove the stored platform key)
  exec <target> <prompt>     Run a hosted mission once and print the answer
  chat                       Chat with a hosted mission in the current Forge project
  project                    Manage portable Forge projects
  publish <reference> <dir>  Package a mission directory into a self-contained OCI artifact and push it
  clean                      Remove cached OCI experts from ~/.forge/experts
  serve <agent>              Serve a mission as an OpenAI-compatible endpoint
  claude <target>            Launch Claude Code talking to a forge mission
  connect                    Wire an editor's Claude Code extension to a forge mission
  agent                      Manage forge agents running in Docker
  webui                      Manage Open WebUI connected to a forge agent
  provider                   Manage LLM provider profiles
  mcp <mission>              Expose a mission as a stdio MCP server (for Claude Desktop and MCP-aware tools)

